## 3. Evidence
(a) the authors specify that the checklist applies “when researchers employ linear fixed effects models” (p. 834), 
and their literature review focuses on studies using linear fixed-effects estimators (p. 830). 
Thus, it would be inaccurate to say that they never specify the scope of their recommendations. 
However, the title and abstract may give readers the impression that the paper addresses the interpretation of fixed-effects results more generally. 
In particular, residualizing the treatment variable and interpreting the effect by multiplying the coefficient by the standard deviation of the residualized variable rely on the structure of a linear model.

